            <ArticleTitle>Primary Breast T Cell Lymphoma Involving Nipple-Areolar Complex in a Young Patient.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>499-501</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1007/s12262-016-1442-9</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We present a rare case of recurrent primary breast lymphoma involving the nipple-areolar complex and review literature on primary breast lymphoma, its clinical presentation and management. It is diagnosed by histopathology. It needs multimodality management protocols.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
